==English==
{{wp}}

===Etymology===
{{ety|en|:bor|la-med:currentia<ety:af<la:currēns><la:-ia<id:abstract noun>>>|:af<surf>|current|-cy|tree=1|text=+}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈkʌɹ.ən.si/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈkʌɹ.ən.si/|/ˈkɝ.ən.si/|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-currency.wav|a=Southern England|IPA=[-nts-]}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-currency.ogg|a=US,hurry-furry|IPA=[-nts-]}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{senseid|en|Q8142}}[[money|Money]] or other items used to facilitate [[transaction]]s.
#: {{ux|en|[[wampum|Wampum]] was used as a '''currency''' by [[Amerindian]]s.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=William G. McBride|title=INVESTING; CHASING RETURNS IN DIFFERENT CURRENCIES|magazine=w:The New York Times|url=https://www.nytimes.com/1986/05/25/business/investing-chasing-returns-in-different-currencies.html|date=25-05-1986|passage=Money managers who play down '''currencies''' tend to argue that outguessing foreign exchange markets in the short term is perilous, and that, over the long haul, shifts in '''currency''' values tend to offset one another.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20150524193614/http://www.nytimes.com/1986/05/25/business/investing-chasing-returns-in-different-currencies.html|archivedate=24 May 2015}}
# {{lb|en|more|_|specifically}} {{U|paper}} [[money]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1943|author=w:William Saroyan|title={{w|The Human Comedy (novel)|The Human Comedy}}|chapter=3
|passage=Spangler went through his pockets, coming out with a handful of small coins, one piece of '''currency''' and a hard-boiled egg.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Richard Collett|title=He ran out of countries to visit, so he created his own|magazine=w:CNN|url=https://www.cnn.com/2023/06/08/travel/slowjamastan-micronation|date=2023-06-08|passage=Two years on, and while the Sultan of Slowjamastan has instigated more than a few bizarre laws (he’s outlawed the wearing of Crocs, for example), the Republic also has all the trappings of a fledgling nation-state. It issues its own passports, flies its own flag, prints its own '''currency''' (“the duble”), and has a national anthem that’s played on state occasions.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260516010746/https://www.cnn.com/2023/06/08/travel/slowjamastan-micronation|archivedate=16 May 2026}}
# The state of being [[current]]; general acceptance, recognition or use.
#: {{ux|en|The [[jargon|jargon’s]] '''currency'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=1983-04-09|journal=w:Gay Community News|page=5|author=Kenneth Hale Wehmann|title=Conscientious Resistance|text=Fear of punishment has no '''currency''' with me as long as I remain convinced of the larger value of what I have done.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} Current value; general estimation; the [[rate]] at which anything is generally valued.
#* {{RQ:Bacon War with Spain|passage=He {{...}} takes greatness of kingdoms according to their bulk and '''currency''', and not after intrinsic value.}}
#* {{RQ:Irving Sketch Book|title=English Writers on America|page=112|passage=The bare name of Englishman {{...}} too often gave a transient '''currency''' to the worthless and ungrateful.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} [[fluency|Fluency]]; readiness of utterance.

