===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|danke|t=wet, damp; dampness, moisture}}, probably from {{der|en|gmq}}, related to {{cog|sv|dank||marshy spot}}, {{cog|is|dökk|t=pool}}, {{cog|non|dǫkk|t=pit, depression}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*dankwaz|t=dark}}. However, some trace it to a {{der|en|gmw}} source such as {{cog|nl|damp||vapor}} or {{cog|gmh|damph}}, both ultimately from {{cog|gem-pro|*dampaz||smoke, steam, vapor}}.<ref>{{R:gem:EDPG}}</ref><ref>{{R:ine:IEW|669}}</ref><ref>{{R:Online_Etymology_Dictionary|dank}}</ref>

Modern slang senses derived from the drug sense; compare {{m|en|based|t=awesome, especially in a right-wing context online}} from drug terminology {{m|en|freebased}}.

