====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|heraldiccharge}} A normally horizontal stripe called a [[fess]] that has been modified to [[zig-zag]] across the center of a [[coat of arms]] from [[dexter]] to [[sinister]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1828|author=Sir Nicholas Harris Nicolas; Walter (of Exeter)|title=The Siege of Carlaverock in the XXVIII Edward I. A. D. MCCC|page=243
|text=The fact appears to have been that Simon de Montacute bore two coats; the one, Argent, three fusils, which it is most probable was a corruption of a fess dancette, or a '''dance''', Gules; and the other, Azure, a griffin segreant{{nb...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1902|title=The Ancestor: A Quarterly Review of County and Family History, Heraldry and Antiquities ...|page=85
|text=It is as follows - being headed by a shield of arms in colours - gold with a '''dance''' gules between three croslets fitchy gules.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1922|title=Miscellanea Genealogica Et Heraldica|page=189
|text=Or, a '''dance''' gules, in chief 3 lions' faces sable.}}

