===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|chemistry}} A cup-shaped piece of [[laboratory]] [[equipment]] used to contain [[chemical]] [[compound]]s when heating them to very high [[temperature]]s.
#* {{quote-book
|en
|title=The Works of the Late Edgar Allan Poe
|chapter=[[s:en:The Works of the Late Edgar Allan Poe/Volume 1/Von Kempelen and His Discovery|Von Kempelen and His Discovery]]
|year=1850
|author=Edgar Allan Poe
|passage=In one corner of the closet was a very small furnace, with a glowing fire in it, and on the fire a kind of duplicate '''crucible'''—two '''crucibles''' connected by a tube. One of these '''crucibles''' was nearly full of lead in a state of fusion, but not reaching up to the aperture of the tube, which was close to the brim.}}
#* {{RQ:Silberman NeuroTribes|chapter=1|page=27|text=He turned the downstairs drawing room into a lab, installing a furnace, '''crucible''', and fume hood, and stocking it with hundreds of beakers, flasks, pipes, and balances.}}
# A [[heat-resistant]] container in which [[metal]]s are [[melted]], usually at temperatures above 500°C, commonly made of [[graphite]] with [[clay]] as a [[binder]].
# The bottom and hottest part of a [[blast furnace]]; the [[hearth]].
# {{lb|en|figuratively}} A very [[difficult]] and [[trying]] [[experience]], that acts as a [[refining]] or [[hardening]] [[process]].
#: {{cot|en|trial by fire}}
#* {{RQ:Landon Ethel Churchill|page=70|volume=II|passage=But, in considering an author and his works as one, a sufficient distinction is not drawn between the ideal and the real: the last is only given by being past through the '''crucible''' of the first.}}
#* {{quote-journal
|en
|date=July 22, 1973
|origdate=July 17, 1973
|author=w:Chiang Kai-shek
|title=President Chiang Kai-shek's message to the mass rally supporting Captive Nations Week
|journal=Free China Weekly
|url=https://archive.org/details/sim_free-china-weekly_1973-07-22_14_28/
|volume=XIV
|issue=28
|location=[[Taipei]]
|issn=0016-0318
|oclc=1786626
|page=1
|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/sim_free-china-weekly_1973-07-22_14_28/
|text=We should give our support to the liberation of the captive nations of the world and deliver our compatriots from their '''crucible''' of suffering. In other words, we should take up the difficult task of reshaping the world’s destiny by destroying the tyrannical Communist rule now afflicting the earth and by delivering humankind from the Red holocaust.}}
#* {{quote-text
|en
|title=Presidential Radio Address
|url={{fullurl:s:en:Presidential Radio Address - 3 July 1982}}
|date=1982-07-03
|author=w:Ronald Reagan
|passage=Some of our ancestors faced trials that we will never know—the snows of Valley Forge; the '''crucible''' of a bitter, bloody civil war; and the incredible hardships endured in taming a savage wilderness.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1999|author={{w|Seamus Heaney}}|title={{w|Beowulf}}|publisher=Faber and Faber|chapter=Introduction|location=London|page=xix|passage=Beowulf's mood as he gets ready to fight the dragon - who could be read as a projection of Beowulf's own chthonic wisdom refined in the '''crucible''' of experience - recalls the mood of other tragic heroes.}}

